<BaseLayout {title} {description} lang="en"><section class="case-intro"><span class="case-no">ARCHITECTURE STORY / 02</span><h1>From zero to a multi-tenant product.</h1><p class="lede">A B2B SaaS platform designed as a product from its first architectural decisions: domain, tenant isolation, security, APIs, web experience and cloud.</p></section><div class="case-facts"><div><small>Starting point</small><strong>0 → SaaS</strong></div><div><small>Architecture</small><strong>Multi-tenant · Domain · Security</strong></div><div><small>Stack</small><strong>Java · Spring Boot · React · GCP</strong></div></div><section class="case-body"><div class="prose"><h2>A product, not client forks.</h2><div><p>The domain contains organizations with different structures and operational needs. The architecture had to preserve tenant isolation without turning every customer into a separate implementation.</p><p>That made multi-tenancy, authorization and domain boundaries product decisions rather than infrastructure details.</p></div></div><div class="system-flow" aria-label="Conceptual SaaS flow"><span class="node">React</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node">API / Access</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node accent">Multi-tenant domain</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node">Data / GCP</span></div><div class="prose"><h2>The architecture lives in the boundaries.</h2><div class="decision-list"><div class="decision"><b>01</b><strong>Multi-tenancy</strong><p>Tenant context is part of the base product model, not a later customization.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>02</b><strong>Domain</strong><p>Business rules and organizational structures modeled around the problem rather than the UI.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>03</b><strong>Security</strong><p>Authentication and role-based authorization integrated into flows and APIs.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>04</b><strong>Hands-on ownership</strong><p>Architecture, backend, frontend, cloud operations and product roadmap remain connected.</p></div></div></div></section></BaseLayout>